      "side": 1,
      "message": "This gives you a raw git branch name, but Read the Docs addresses versions by *slug*, and every downstream use of $branch passes it through unslugified.\n\nlftools-uv 0.8.2 added `--from-branch` to project-version-details, project-version-update and project-build-trigger for exactly this case. version_slug() (lftools_uv/api/endpoints/readthedocs.py:115) lowercases and replaces every character outside [a-z0-9._-] with a hyphen, so `stable/scandium` becomes `stable-scandium`. Without the flag the argument is used verbatim -- see typer_apps/rtd.py:322, 364 and 465, each of which is `target \u003d version_slug(x) if from_branch else x` -- and the request path becomes `projects/X/versions/stable/scandium/`, which 404s. lftools-uv\u0027s own docstring uses `maintenance/3.7.10` as the example, so this is a case the library explicitly expects callers to hit.\n\nTo be clear this is not a regression: legacy lftools never checked HTTP status at all, so today this hangs in watchbuild until the Jenkins job timeout instead of failing. The new code failing fast is strictly better. But the fix is one flag and it is already in the version you pin, so it seems a shame to carry the bug forward.\n\nAffects rtd_version_state on L250 and L261, watchbuild on L258, and project-version-update on L264.\n\nRelated: tests/shell/test-rtdv3.sh only exercises GERRIT_BRANCH values `master`, `London` and `london` (L50, L225, L238). A branch containing a slash would be a worthwhile case to add, since that is the one this change alters the failure mode for.",
      "tag": "code-review",
      "revId": "7f755204586d70cc76c98c9abf6a689af35e1bb2",
      "serverId": "f2a2391d-0403-4fa5-b183-4056999a8a09"
    },
